  "title": "Christopher Columbus",
  "summary": "Christopher Columbus, a Genoese explorer born in 1451, sailed west across the Atlantic from Spain in 1492 and sighted land on October 12. He made four voyages to the Caribbean region. Those he enslaved suffered torture, killing and European diseases. People lived in the Americas long before him; the Mariners' Museum says his real achievement was opening the door to more exploration. He died in Valladolid in 1506.",
